11:["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-16 rounded-2xl border bg-card p-6 shadow-soft","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-lg font-semibold","children":"About voice-activated SOS"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":"Web browsers cannot listen to the microphone when a tab is closed or the phone is locked, so locked-screen voice detection will ship in the native Android app. It uses on-device keyword spotting in a foreground service with a visible notification, and never uploads raw audio. In the web app you can configure your phrase, test your microphone while the page is open, and run a clearly labelled simulated trigger. Even on Android, OS battery restrictions mean background detection can never be guaranteed, so manual SOS always remains available."}]]}]
